<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 3D Helmholtz/Turing standing-wave eigenmodes and proximodistal 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal chondrogenesis in developing Gallus gallus wing bud — Code-to-model traceability: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring (L1-93) maps the Pass 3 model and Lean Theorems 4-6 to their sources; the Section 4b header (L562-600) is an explicit honest-scope statement listing what is and is not a finite-element / paddle-outline model; function docstrings cite Hentschel 2004, Zhu 2010, Sun 2002, Boehm 2010, Summerbell 1974/1977 and Rowe & Fallon 1982 at the point of use; the Math KG spec now registers 6 laws with Lean loci and code loci (`newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.yaml`, L1-143)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 3D Helmholtz/Turing standing-wave eigenmodes and proximodistal 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal chondrogenesis in developing Gallus gallus wing bud — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Retains the exact Newman & Frisch (1979) Eqs. (1)-(7) dispersion relation (`compute_newman_dispersion`, L161-271) and the 1D/2D nonlinear DCT-II IMEX solvers (L274-468). Pass 3 adds the requested 3D moving boundary (L847-1152): Lagrangian P1 FEM in z with advection a(z) = int S dz, dilution and bisection refinement (L1045-1108), a moving distal boundary, DST-II Dirichlet dorsal/ventral ectoderm (L898), active-zone kinetics with k_PD^2 from the actual discrete PD operator (L668-692) and fu chosen by bisection so the fastest linear mode is exactly m^2 + k_DV^2 + k_PD^2 (L695-770), plus three new Lean theorems (Helmholtz budget, FGF8 window depth, Hill-2 monotonicity). It is held at 94 rather than raised because the remediation exposed structural limits: (i) pattern selection is not growth-sensitive — the S_max = 0 sweep run (zero outgrowth) still yields [1, 2, 3] (L1204-1209), so the moving boundary sets element lengths only; (ii) the Table 1 map m(L_PD) (L186-191) is still an empirical input and the m-increment joint/interzone is an imposed field reset (L1006-1012); (iii) the AP/DV cross-section is spectral on a box (header L567-600), not a FEM mesh of the paddle-shaped bud; (iv) post-excision kinetics are held by rule (L991-997)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L1006–L1012: Joint/interzone on m increment is an imposed reset of the active + apical field to noise (documented, not emergent) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L1006-L1012>",
        "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L1204–L1209: S_max sweep: S = 0 (no outgrowth) still produces [1, 2, 3] — element count is clock-set, growth-insensitive <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L1204-L1209>",
        "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L186–L191: Table 1 mode map m(L_PD) thresholds 375/190/125 um remain an empirical input to the kinetics (not derived from hyaluronate -> D_eff) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L186-L191>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 3D Helmholtz/Turing standing-wave eigenmodes and proximodistal 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal chondrogenesis in developing Gallus gallus wing bud — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1671-1836) now reports 14 reference-backed measurements: the 8 Pass 2 items (unchanged values) plus 3D record total elements 6 vs 6, L_PD(24 h) 250.2 vs 250 um, L_PD(48 h) 128.6 vs 140 um (-8.1 %, the 3-point clock fit's residual), excision at 0 h -> 1 vs 1, excision at 24 h -> 3 vs 3, and record AP spacing ratio 1.484 vs 1.5. The L_PD(48 h) miss and the fact that the excision series is partly a consequence of the imposed m-map timing keep this below the mid-90s." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L639–L665: Hyaluronidase clock fit to Table 1 (tau_H = 37.0 h) — L_PD(48 h) = 128.6 um vs 140 um reference is an 8 % residual of the one-parameter exponential <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L639-L665>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-3d-moving-boundary-intact-aer-total-skeletal-elements-in-the-frozen-record-1-2-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-3d-record-zeugopod-to-autopod-anteroposterior-spacing-ratio-m-2-m-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-equal-diffusion-du-dv-and-hyaluronate-excess-fu-1-5-negative-control-amplitude>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh20-stylopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-500-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh24-zeugopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-250-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh27-chick-wing-autopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-140-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh28-chick-hindlimb-autopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-115-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-intact-aer-2d-wing-bud-total-skeletal-elements-stylopod-1-zeugopod-2-autopod-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-active-progress-zone-depth-l-pd-at-24-h-hh24>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-active-progress-zone-depth-l-pd-at-48-h-hh27>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-aer-excision-at-t-0-h-hh20-cumulative-skeletal-elements>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-aer-excision-at-t-24-h-hh24-cumulative-skeletal-elements>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-progress-zone-mode-number-l-ap-lambda-ap-vs-pde-element-count-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-segmented-gallus-gallus-wing-specimen-zeugopod-to-autopod-spacing-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-morphometric-validation-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

